<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's J. Martins sees sales up 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal's J. Martins sees sales up 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese retailer Jeronimo Martins expects sales to have risen 25 percent in 1996 to 350 billion escudos, company director Nogueira de Brito was quoted as saying on Thursday.</p>
<p>De Brito told Diario Economico that the company had succeeded in quadrupling sales over the past seven years.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
